# Fixture 3: retransmitted identical CF (kept as evidence, no data duplication) vs
# same sequence index with conflicting payload (hard conflict, later never overwrites).
#
# 20-byte ReadDataByIdentifier response; CF index 1 arrives twice identically.
0   7E0 TX 03 22 F1 90 00 00 00 00
5   7E8 RX 10 14 62 F1 90 41 55 44
15  7E0 TX 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
25  7E8 RX 21 49 56 31 32 33 34 35
# retransmit of index 1, same bytes: accepted as evidence only
28  7E8 RX 21 49 56 31 32 33 34 35
45  7E8 RX 22 36 37 38 39 30 41 42
#
# Conflict scenario: 20-byte response where index 1 changes payload mid-transfer.
200 7E0 TX 03 22 F1 8C 00 00 00 00
205 7E8 RX 10 14 62 F1 8C 01 02 03
215 7E0 TX 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
225 7E8 RX 21 04 05 06 07 08 09 0A
# same index 1 with different payload while transfer still open -> ISO_SEQUENCE_CONFLICT
245 7E8 RX 21 FF EE DD CC BB AA 99
